# Line endings for this repository.
#
# Git already stores every text file here with LF — `git ls-files --eol` finds
# no CRLF in the index. What it did NOT say was how to check one out, so a
# clone on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working tree,
# and `bun run format:check` then fails on 1 211 files: Prettier expects LF.
#
# That is the worst shape a gate can have — red for whoever is working, green
# for whoever is reviewing — because it is indistinguishable from a real
# formatting error and there is nothing a person can fix in their own change.
#
# `eol=lf` beats `core.autocrlf`, so it fixes this for everyone who clones
# rather than asking each person to configure their machine. The same file
# exists in allfitone-design-system, for the same reason and in the same shape.
#
# NOTE: adding this file does not rewrite a working tree that is already CRLF.
# To convert an existing clone once: `git add --renormalize .`
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never looks at the bytes. Images are the reason this list
# exists: a PNG can contain a CR+LF pair by coincidence, and `text=auto`
# classifies it by its NUL bytes rather than by that pair. Saying it here does
# not change today's behaviour — it makes the next image or font format
# somebody commits safe without anybody having to know the heuristic.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# SVG is text, and deliberately not in the list above: it is diffed and read as
# text, and it must be LF.
